<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner wins NOK 380 mln HK office deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins NOK 380 mln HK office deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian shipbuilding and construction group Kvaerner ASA said on Tuesday its subsidiary Gammon Construction Ltd had won a 380 million crown contract to build an office block in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Gammon Construction is part of Kvaerner Construction.</p>
<p>The project, called Lincoln House, is part of a larger construction known as Tai Koo Place, and will comprise a 24-floor office block with a five-storey car park.</p>
<p>It is due to be completed in June 1998.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
